`tests/conftest.py::unprivileged_dsn` already exists for precisely this. It is **session-scoped**, so
a module-scoped fixture can request it, and it provisions `recall_rls_probe`
(`NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS`), granting it the connected role's privileges. Take it and pass it as
`RECALL_DSN`.

```python
@pytest.fixture(scope="module")
def live_server(tmp_path_factory, unprivileged_dsn):
    env = {..., "RECALL_DSN": unprivileged_dsn}
```
